Renewal and cancellation (INS-REN-05)

Issuer: Poisťovňa Devín, a. s. · IČO 00 682 447 · Pribinova 10, 811 09 Bratislava

A renewal offer goes out at least 30 to 60 days before the anniversary, depending on the product rules, and shows last year's premium next to the new one.
Either party may terminate an annual policy by written notice delivered at least six weeks before the anniversary, as the Civil Code provides; a non-renewal notice states the reason where the product rules require it.
A new contract may be cancelled within two months of conclusion by either party, and the insurer is entitled to a proportionate part of the premium.
Non-payment: the contract lapses when the premium is unpaid after the statutory grace period following a written reminder, and the reminder must state that consequence.
For motor third-party liability, termination is reported to the Slovak Insurers' Bureau, and the certificate of claims history is issued to the client on request.
Mid-term changes are confirmed by endorsement before the risk changes, never afterwards.

